\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Christ, whose glory fills the skies,
\par Christ, the true, the only Light,
\par Sun of Righteousness, arise,
\par Triumph o'er the shades of night;
\par Day- spring from on high, be near;
\par Day- star, in my heart appear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Dark and cheerless is the morn
\par Unaccompanied by Thee:
\par Joyless is the day's return,
\par Till Thy mercy's beams I see,
\par Till Thou inward light impart,
\par Glad my eyes, and warm my heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Visit then this soul of mine;
\par Pierce the gloom of sin and grief;
\par Fill me, Radiancy divine;
\par Scatter all my unbelief;
\par More and more Thyself display,
\par Shining to the perfect day.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

